  "id": "COMPOUND:145 - PROTEIN:519",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Dihomo-gamma-linolenic acid may be associated with Protein-arginine deiminase type-3 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Dihomo-gamma-linolenic acid to Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6, which in turn targets Protein-arginine deiminase type-3. The second pathway connects Dihomo-gamma-linolenic acid to Tissue factor pathway inhibitor, which is targeted by alpha-Linolenic acid, which also targets Protein-arginine deiminase type-3. These findings indicate that Dihomo-gamma-linolenic acid may influence the activity of Protein-arginine deiminase type-3 through a series of molecular interactions involving other lipid and protein targets. The evidence supports a potential role for Dihomo-gamma-linolenic acid in modulating the activity of this enzyme, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the relationships are indirect and involve multiple layers of molecular interactions.",
